From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Ross <jonross@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:55:48 -0700
Subject: gpu: Verify context restore after using the passthrough shared
 context

Passthrough decoder commands that temporarily make the lazy shared
context current did not check whether making it current succeeded, or
whether the decoder's own context was restored afterwards.

Add ScopedSharedContextCurrent, which makes the shared context current
and on destruction verifies that the decoder's context is current again.
Pixel local storage is only interrupted and restored when the decoder's
context was current. If the decoder's context is not current afterwards,
it is marked lost and no further GL calls are made. Commands also lose
the context if the shared context cannot be made current.

Bug: 557605839
Change-Id: I2db2fe87be73b385df4ac8ab8e889e755fcc13d8
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8519645
Commit-Queue: Jonathan Ross <jonross@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1714011}

